#!/bin/sh
# A fake `nvcc` that reports a version and compiles nothing.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `llvq-cuda` is gated `cfg(target_os = "linux")`, so the
# development Mac never type-checks `bin/planesbench.rs` or the other CUDA
# sources — and that gap has already cost this project a day: `DISPLAY_NAMES`
# was left seven literals short of `N_ARMS` on 2026-08-15 and only surfaced on
# 2026-08-16, in a build launched for something else. See the comment on
# `arms::DISPLAY_NAMES`.
#
# `cargo check --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` would close that gap, but
# `cudarc`'s build script probes `nvcc --version` and panics without it. It only
# probes the VERSION: `cargo check` neither compiles device code nor links, so a
# stub is enough to type-check the whole linux-gated tree on a Mac.
#
#   PATH="$PWD/ops/devtools:$PATH" \
#     cargo clippy -p llvq-cuda --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --all-targets
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A TYPE CHECK, NOT A BUILD. It proves the Rust compiles; it says
# nothing about whether NVRTC accepts the kernel text, whether a kernel spills,
# or whether anything computes the right thing. Only a card answers those.
# Never put this directory on PATH for anything but `cargo check`/`clippy`.
cat <<'V'
nvcc: NVIDIA (R) Cuda compiler driver
Copyright (c) 2005-2024 NVIDIA Corporation
Cuda compilation tools, release 12.4, V12.4.99
Build cuda_12.4.r12.4/compiler.33961263_0
V
